\": \"华法令 is associated with severe adverse reactions, including 出血危象 (hemorrhagic crisis), 出血并发症 (bleeding complications), and 抗凝血控制障碍 (anticoagulation control disorder). Evidence indicates that even minor reductions in plasma protein binding (e.g., from 98% to 96%) can double 华法令’s pharmacological activity, leading to fatal hemorrhage. In one study, 78 out of 500 hospitalized patients on 华法令 experienced bleeding, with 20 cases linked to drug interactions. Additionally, chemotherapy agents like ifosfamide have triggered severe anticoagulation control disorders in patients on 华法令. [Data: Relationships (9458, 9459, 9461)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Androgenic/anabolic steroids interact with 华法令 via shared metabolic pathways\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Drugs such as 甲基睾丸素, 去甲乙基睾酮, and 雄性醇—all classified as androgenic or anabolic steroids—interact with 华法令. 甲基睾丸素 is metabolized by hepatic microsomal enzymes and is susceptible to enzyme-inducing agents like phenobarbital, which also affect 华法令 metabolism. Although direct interaction mechanisms between these steroids and 华法令 are not fully detailed in all cases, their inclusion in lists of drugs whose metabolism is accelerated by enzyme inducers suggests potential for reduced 华法令 efficacy if co-administered with such inducers. However, some steroids may also displace 华法令 from protein binding, increasing free drug levels. [Data: Entities (6972, 4081, 9215); Relationships (49610, 31848, 53955)]\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 8.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The community poses high clinical impact due to the life-threatening bleeding risks and complex drug interactions associated with 华法令, a widely used anticoagulant requiring precise monitoring.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1782127179, "model": "